{"title":"2022 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Three identical squares form rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/0/2b076f2e7f124fc5d8b5ef7b30b95bfcfe85449f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WXYZ$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" />, as shown\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>The perimeter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/0/2b076f2e7f124fc5d8b5ef7b30b95bfcfe85449f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WXYZ$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" /> is 56 m. The area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/0/2b076f2e7f124fc5d8b5ef7b30b95bfcfe85449f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WXYZ$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/1/25182eff81179585b9f47d3581f500f783d02bf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 66 \\text{ m}^{2} \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 147 \\text{ m}^{2} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 168 \\text{ m}^{2} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 196 \\text{ m}^{2} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 348 \\text{ m}^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"567\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the side length of each square. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/0/2b076f2e7f124fc5d8b5ef7b30b95bfcfe85449f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WXYZ$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" /> is made up of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> identical squares, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/1/d511c45fbd8db0e465256439f7dedb39bdf174dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WX = 3x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/9/339b5d0956ad7c080a33ec5e510f9b93b8ed4573.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XY = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"68\" height=\"14\" />. The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Perimeter\" title=\"Perimeter\">perimeter</a> of a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Rectangle\" title=\"Rectangle\">rectangle</a> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times the sum of its side lengths, so we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/9/8f9d1ad779a4318504b7764e469bfd98bc6a2b04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(3x + x) = 56$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"120\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/9/b49420ef59df2e0a702189d3fae9df333f7f5d45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 4x = 56$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/4/9340181567642b4a9de18c815ed703da116c8aa5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8x = 56$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/2/6f250e9e4277021523f5d5ec16f656bbd4a6329e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{56}{8} = 7 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"111\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/7/5c74fac7f398636958810c7d39013e4aba8f9276.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WX = 3 \\times 7 = 21 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"164\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Area\" title=\"Area\">area</a> of a rectangle is equal to the product of its side lengths, so the area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/a/a5ab06c9539935721c241136e9fb180ea1a2226f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7 \\times 21 = \\boxed{\\textbf {(B) } 147 \\text{ m}^{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"176\" height=\"32\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher \n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"2022 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">2022 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2022 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2022 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a